  "_us_twin_cities_note": "'Dublin, CA | Remote' hard-failed because 'dublin' (Ireland) is in location_fail_any. A fail-list city named here is ignored in a segment that also names one of these US states. Two-letter codes match UPPERCASE only, so 'Toronto, CA' (Canada) never counts, and any other fail-list hit in the segment (a country) still blocks.",
  "endorsed_exact_zip_prefixes": {},
  "_endorsed_exact_zip_prefixes_note": "An endorsed exact segment matches after its ZIP, street address, work-style words ('Hybrid', 'Office'), uppercase state code and country words are stripped, so 'New York, US, 10003' and 'New York - Hybrid' are the segment 'new york', while 'New York - Albany' is not. This maps an exact segment to the ZIP prefixes that name it, so a segment holding only a ZIP and a state code can match, for example {\"new york\": [\"100\", \"101\", \"102\", \"103\", \"104\"]}. Empty here because the example candidate endorses no exact segment.",
