  "_title_hard_exclude_note": "Titles that ARE an out-of-scope role, as case-insensitive regexes on the normalised title. They run on the in-lane path only, and only when the rest of the gate kept the req, so the blast radius is exactly the kept reqs that now fail (reason 'title excluded (<family>): <match>'). Each family carries its own except list: the second marketing family ('Global Integrated Marketing Programs Lead', 'Growth Marketing Strategy Manager', 'Field Marketing Manager') spares a title that also names product, program or project management or ownership, or TPM ('Program Manager, Partner Marketing', 'Marketing Program Manager'). Whole words: 'Wholesale' never matches 'sales'. Empty the list to turn it off.",
  "snapshot_keep_days": 60,
  "_snapshot_keep_days_note": "A full sweep deletes dated snapshots (data/snapshot_<date>.json[.gz]) older than this many days. latest.json and the two newest dated snapshots always stay. 0 keeps every snapshot.",
  "candidate_profile": "examples/john_doe/candidate.json",
  "form_min_score": 60,
  "gh_detail_max_fetch": 150,
  "_candidate_profile_note": "The candidate's facts (years, home, relocation markets, work authorization, degree, certifications, clearance, people management) as JSON, relative to the repo root. Greenhouse's job-detail call returns each posting's application form; the sweep reads it for scored Greenhouse postings at form_min_score or above and --form-check reads it on demand, and every question is compared against this file: KNOCKOUT (the truthful answer likely auto-rejects), ASK (needs the candidate's judgment) or OK. A flag for the person deciding, never a gate or a score input. The same call fills a missing pay band from pay_input_ranges. gh_detail_max_fetch caps those calls per sweep. Remove candidate_profile to skip form reads; pay bands are still filled.",
